Kruger National Park sits in north-eastern South Africa, along Mozambique's border to the east, from Zimbabwe to the north and the Crocodile River at the southern border.
The park comprises 19,500 Km2 and is divided in 14 different ecological zones, each supporting different animal species.
It's one of South Africa's main attractions and is considered to be the flagship of South African National Parks (SANParks).
There are fees for park admission and conservation, just as it is with all national parks in South Africa.
It may also be very useful to acquire a Wild Card. With it you can have access to several South African parks or all South African national parks.
